00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,220
Using language Reading and listening

2
00:00:06,180 --> 00:00:07,880
The story of Atlanta

3
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:10,820
Atlanta was a Greek princess.

4
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:15,620
She was very beautiful and could run faster than any man in Greece.

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:20,840
But she was not allowed to run and win glory for herself in the Olympic Games.

6
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,520
Her father said that she must marry,

7
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:33,820
so Atlanta made a bargain with him.

8
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:38,420
She said to him, "These are my rules.

9
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:41,360
When a man says he wants to marry me,

10
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:43,060
I will run against him.

11
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,520
If he cannot run as fast as me.

12
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:46,640
he will be killed.

13
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:59,060
So many of them sadly went home,

14
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:01,120
but others stayed to run the race.

15
00:01:02,210 --> 00:01:06,840
There was a man called Hippomenes who was amazed when he heard of Atlanta’s rules, "

16
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:11,180
Why are these men so foolish?" he thought.

17
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:15,820
Why will they let themselves be killed because they cannot run as fast as this princess?"

18
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:17,360
However,

19
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:20,400
when he saw Atlanta come out of her house to run,

20
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:22,560
Hippomenes changed his mind.

21
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,940
I will marry Atlanta - or die!" he said.

22
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:32,360
The race started and although the men ran very fast,

23
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:33,880
Atlanta ran faster.

24
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:37,300
As Hippomenes watched he thought, "

25
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:43,820
How can I run as fast as Atlanta?" He went to ask the Greek Goddess of Love

26
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:48,380
for help.She promised to help him and gave him three golden apples.

27
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:54,480
She said, "Throw an apple in front of Atlanta when she is running past.

28
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:58,780
When she stops to pick it up, you will be able to run past her

29
00:01:58,780 --> 00:02:03,340
and win." Hippomenes took the apples and went to the King.

30
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:10,480
He said, "I want to marry Atlanta." The King was sad to see another man die,

31
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:17,680
but Hippomenes said, "I will marry her - or die!" So the race began.
